<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Salomon keeps Xerox at buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Salomon keeps Xerox at buy.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Salomon Brothers said it maintained a buy rating on Xerox Corp despite the breakdown of its deal to sell its insurance unit to  Kohlberg Kravis Roberts &amp; Co.</p>
<p>-- Said sees minimal impact from deal cancellation.</p>
<p>Trimmed 1997 earnings estimate to $4.11-$4.15 per share range from $4.18 per share based on expected small slowdown in rate of share repurchases.  </p>
<p>-- Revised price target to $60-65 range from $65-70 range.</p>
<p>-- Shares fell three to 54-7/8.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730</p>
</text>
